<Base
  title="How we verify compatibility"
  description="Where Workswithwhat's compatibility data comes from, what each status means, and how we handle conflicting or missing information."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'How we verify', path: '/methodology/' }]}
>
  <h1>How we verify compatibility</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A “works with” answer is only useful if you can check it. So each one on this site points to the page it came from.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
  <p>In order of preference:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>The manufacturer's own product page, datasheet, manual or support article.</li>
    <li>The Connectivity Standards Alliance certification database, for Matter.</li>
    <li>Platform pages from Apple, Google, Amazon, Samsung SmartThings and Home Assistant.</li>
    <li>Retailers and independent reviews, only to back up one of the above.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Two passes per device</h2>
  <p>
    One pass collects the specs and sources. A second pass goes through every claim again on its own and checks
    that the cited page actually says it, for that exact model and region. Anything that doesn't hold up is marked
    <span class="badge s-unknown">Unconfirmed</span> instead of guessed. A device appears on the site only after the second pass.
  </p>

  <h2>What the labels mean</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="badge s-native">Yes</span> Works through the brand's own integration: an Alexa skill, Google Home linking, HomeKit or an official Home Assistant integration.</li>
    <li><span class="badge s-matter">Yes, via Matter</span> Works because the plug is Matter-certified. You add it with the platform's Matter pairing. Thread plugs also need a Thread border router, such as a recent Apple TV, HomePod mini or Nest Hub.</li>
    <li><span class="badge s-hub">Via …</span> Works, but only through the named hub or bridge.</li>
    <li><span class="badge s-no">No</span> A source says it isn't supported.</li>
    <li><span class="badge s-unknown">Unconfirmed</span> We couldn't find an official answer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Regions and versions</h2>
  <p>
    The US and EU versions of a plug often have different model numbers, radios or certifications. We treat them as
    separate devices and list the regions each record covers.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Firmware updates change compatibility all the time. If something here is wrong or out of date,
    <a href="https://github.com/miguelvalera/workswithwhat/issues">open an issue</a> with a link, and we'll re-check it.
    No brand pays to be listed, and there are no affiliate links.
  </p>
</Base>
